      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately that the tBLE_ADDR_TYPE used in tSMB_CB for the identity address type has all of these address types mixed together.\n\nIt\u0027s hard to tell what possible values p_cb-\u003eid_addr_type in smp_act.cc can have. Are you sure it\u0027s just 0 and 1? The confusing part is the spec defines public, random, public ID, and random ID in a few places (mostly associated with advertising reports), and in those cases both public and public ID are options for public identity address (where the 2nd value of 2 corresponds to resolved RPA).",
